    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="7">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIEm">III Em</ref> 7</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-q">Et omnis homo credibiles faciat homines suos et omnes qui in pace et terra sua sunt.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="7" corresp="#wit-q">Et omnis homo credibiles faciat homines suos et omnes qui in pace et terra sua sunt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q">And every man shall act as surety for his men and for all those who are under his protection and on his estate.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="191"><ref target="clause:IIIAs_7">III As 7</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. III As. 7</note>
        <note type="editorial">Latin only; no German translation in Liebermann. Liebermann compares III As 7.</note>
      </div>
